<title>HONG KONG: Hanil Bank H.K. seen in HK$500 mln FRCD.</title>
<headline>Hanil Bank H.K. seen in HK$500 mln FRCD.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hong Kong branch of South Korea's Hanil Bank has mandated Chase Manhattan Asia to arrange a HK$500 million floating rate certificate of deposit (FRCD) issue, industry sources said.</p>
<p>They said the facility will be swapped into US dollars.</p>
<p>The 364-day issue will be priced at par to float at 17 basis points over the London Interbank Offered Rate.</p>
<p>The management fee for top-tier managers is eight basis points, sources noted.</p>
<p>The deal will be put in general syndication next month.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2847 4039</p>
